  "notes": "{航海|こうかい} refers to travel by sea, especially long-distance ocean voyages. It combines {航|こう} (navigate) + {海|かい} (sea).\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n- No standard transitive pair\n- Pattern: {航海|こうかい}する\n\nCOMMON COMPOUNDS:\n- {航海|こうかい}{士|し}: navigator, ship's officer\n- {航海|こうかい}{日誌|にっし}: ship's log, navigation log\n- {航海|こうかい}{術|じゅつ}: navigation skills/art of navigation\n- {大航海|だいこうかい}{時代|じだい}: Age of Exploration\n- {遠洋|えんよう}{航海|こうかい}: ocean voyage, deep-sea navigation\n- {処女|しょじょ}{航海|こうかい}: maiden voyage\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {航海|こうかい}に{出|で}る: to set sail, to embark on a voyage\n- {航海|こうかい}する: to sail, to navigate\n\nHOMOPHONES:\nこうかい has many homophones in Japanese — be careful with kanji:\n- {後悔|こうかい}: regret\n- {公開|こうかい}: public release/disclosure\n- {公海|こうかい}: high seas, international waters",
